---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { scenes } from '../../../config/images';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import ChartGrammar from '../../../components/ChartGrammar.astro';
import { planets } from '../../../data/planets';
const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Explore Astrology', href: '/explore/' },
  { label: 'The Planets', href: '/explore/planets/' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Planets: functions and drives in a birth chart"
  description="In astrology, planets describe functions and drives: identity, needs, thought, relationship, action, growth, limits, and more. Learn them in context, not as isolated labels."
  path="/explore/planets/"
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} />
  <section class="hero hero--split">
    <div class="container">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Explore Astrology</p>
        <h1>The planets answer: what is happening?</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          In astrology, planets describe functions or drives: ways a person thinks, feels, acts,
          relates, grows, limits, transforms, and makes meaning. Everyone has every planet. What
          changes is how each function is placed, conditioned, and connected to the rest of the chart.
        </p>
      </div>
      <img class="hero__img" src={scenes.planets.src} srcset={scenes.planets.srcset} sizes="100vw" alt={scenes.planets.alt} width={scenes.planets.width} height={scenes.planets.height} fetchpriority="high" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <ChartGrammar active="planet" />

      <div class="prose flow" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-8);">
        <h2>Learn the function before the details</h2>
        <p>
          A planet is not a personality verdict. It is one part of a much larger system. Mars may
          describe assertion or pursuit, but the sign tells us how that function expresses, the
          house tells us where it is operating, and aspects show what other functions participate.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Use this page as a function map:</strong> choose the job you want to understand, then add context.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="function-list">
        {planets.map((p) => (
          <a class="function-row" href={`/explore/planets/${p.slug}/`}>
            <span class="function-row__glyph" aria-hidden="true">{p.glyph}</span>
            <span>
              <strong>{p.name}</strong>
              <span>{p.drive}</span>
            </span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container prose flow">
      <h2>Nothing works alone</h2>
      <p>
        After you know the planet's function, ask three more questions: <a href="/explore/signs/">how</a>
        is it expressing, <a href="/explore/houses/">where</a> is it operating, and what
        <a href="/explore/aspects/">relationships</a> connect it to the rest of the chart? Some
        traditions also use <a href="/explore/dignities/">essential dignities</a> to evaluate a
        planet's condition. The useful question is rarely "What does my Venus mean?" in isolation.
        It is "What is Venus doing here, and how does it belong to the larger pattern?"
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .function-list {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .function-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    align-items: start;
    padding: var(--space-5);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color, currentColor);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg, 1rem);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .function-row__glyph {
    font-size: 2rem;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .function-row strong,
  .function-row span span {
    display: block;
  }

  .function-row span span {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .function-list {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
</style>
